.TH GETSERVBYNAME_R 3
.SH NAME
getservbyname_r, getservbyport_r, getservent_r \- reentrant network services database lookups
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netdb.h>
.PP
.BI "int getservbyname_r(const char *" name ", const char *" proto ,
.BI "struct servent *" ret ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct servent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getservbyport_r(int " port ", const char *" proto ,
.BI "struct servent *" ret ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ", struct servent **" result ");"
.br
.BI "int getservent_r(struct servent *" ret ", char *" buf ", size_t " buflen ,
.BI "struct servent **" result ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are the reentrant equivalents of
.BR getservbyname (3),
.BR getservbyport (3)
and
.BR getservent (3).
The matching
.I /etc/services
entry is copied into the caller-supplied
.I ret
structure and scratch buffer
.IR buf
(length
.IR buflen );
.I *result
points at
.I ret
on success or is NULL when no entry matches.
.I proto
restricts the match to a protocol name
.RB ( """tcp""" ", " """udp""" )
or is NULL to match any.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return 0 on success, or ERANGE if
.I buf
is too small.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ERANGE
.I buf
was too small to hold the result.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getservent (3),
.BR getprotobyname_r (3),
.BR gethostbyname_r (3)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
